This looks like a chemical diagram of rhenium carbonyl complexes and a CO2 conversion reaction. The repeated formula fragments read like Re–Cl–(CO)3 bound to a diimine ligand (the "N N" likely represents a bipyridine/phenanthroline-type ligand). CO2 and CO also appear, so the page is probably depicting a Re(I) tricarbonyl diimine complex used in CO2 reduction (photocatalytic or electrocatalytic) that converts CO2 to CO.

Quick legend:
- Re = rhenium
- Cl = chloride ligand
- CO = carbonyl ligand
- N N = diimine ligand (e.g., bipyridine)
- CO2 = carbon dioxide
- CO = carbon monoxide
- "CT" might refer to charge transfer or "catalyst" in this context

